      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Neighborhoods with recent and concentrated immigrant arrivals often exhibit distinct cultural and socioeconomic characteristics that may foretell systemic risk. For example, neighborhoods with strong informal economies or resident supranational networks may exhibit higher civic engagement, organization, and community solidarity, potentially mitigating negative impacts on stability. Conversely, differences in language barriers, education attainment, poverty rates, and credit-worthiness among new arrivals may signal increased financial resilience or strain.",
